  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Accordion-folded book housed in a wooden box designed as a front door that opens with a ribbon pull tab. Illustrations are of household tools or utensils which are meant to represent family members--hammer represents father, spatula represents mother, screwdriver represents brother, scissors represents sister. These four tools are overlaid on dictionary-style definitions of each family member. The book suggests that the family unit has preconceived gender and sex roles for each family member, which serve as a tool of socialization and sterotype beyond the family.</subfield>
  </datafield>
